WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.700
With the stellar success of the Iron Man film
franchise, it's easy to forget that the Golden

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.980
Avenger wasn't always the major player in
the Marvel Universe that he is now.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.460
The character's never exactly been a C-lister,
but until Robert Downey Jr. infused the role

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.630
with his irresistible humor and charisma,
you couldn't exactly call him an A-lister

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.130
either.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.380
Because so much of the superhero's popularity
is based on the films, it's easy to forget

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.220
how much the source material differs from
what you've seen on the big screen.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.460
So as a little reminder, here's the untold
truth of Iron Man.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.360
A different setting

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.660
The opening scene of 2008's Iron Man is set
in Afghanistan, where Tony Stark is showcasing

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.120
his weapons technology.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.120
But most Americans probably didn't even know
the name "Afghanistan" in 1963.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:55.740
Instead, Tony Stark's origin in Tales of Suspense
#39 was set in a more recognizable locale

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.900
to readers of that time: Vietnam.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.480
According to Stan Lee, his goals for the story
of Tony Stark made Vietnam a fitting setting.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.020
Lee knew exactly who the Marvel readership
was and he wanted to create a character that

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.440
challenged both himself and his readers.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.720
"I'm gonna come up with a character who represents
everything everybody hates and I'm gonna shove

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.760
it down their throats."

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.040
A boy and his dog

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.040
If you only know Iron Man from the movies,
you may be surprised to learn that, for the

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.660
majority of his existence, Stark kept his
superheroic identity a secret.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:35.440
To the rest of the world, Iron Man was actually
Tony Stark's bodyguard, a nameless good samaritan

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.400
keeping the super-rich Stark safe.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.620
"Do you honestly expect us to believe that
he was just a bodyguard in a suit that conveniently

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.200
appeared?

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.580
Despite the fact that…

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.740
"I know that it's confusing."

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:53.440
Iron Man didn't reveal his true identity until
2002's Iron Man #400, when he donned his armor

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.860
in public without any attempt to hide.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.980
Despite what you might think, it wasn't because
of a villain's blackmail or anything; he just

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.200
did it to save a dog.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.810
In the story, Stark notices a dog about to
get hit by a bank robber's car and leaps into

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.120
the fray at the cost of his secret identity.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.660
Now that's a lucky pooch.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.600
"Truth is..."

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.540
"I am Iron Man."

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.560
You're Fired!

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.380
For a CEO and billionaire, Tony Stark isn't
great at keeping jobs.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:34.440
In 2004's Iron Man #78, Tony Stark was confirmed
as the United States Secretary of Defense.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.620
His appointment was short-lived, however.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:41.160
As part of the Avengers Disassembled event
which featured the Scarlet Witch using her

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.720
powers to destroy the team, Stark found himself
magically drunk at the podium of the UN.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.960
The drunk Stark became quickly enraged and
threatened a visiting politician.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.900
Even for politics, threatening visiting dignitaries
with laser blasts was just a step too far,

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.860
and he soon lost the cabinet position.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.180
Seems fair.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.080
But that wouldn't be his last high-profile
appointment.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.720
In 2007, at the end of Civil War #7, Stark
was named Director of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.680
Unfortunately, he would lose that position
by 2009, following Secret Invasion.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.540
Making matters worse, he got replaced by Norman
Osborn, the Green Goblin.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.140
How embarrassing.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.800
How would you feel about getting replaced
by this guy?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.760
"YOU KNOW HOW MUCH I'VE SACRIFICED?"

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:26.920
Yeesh.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.480
Fighting Hawkeye

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.420
Iron Man is a founding member of the Avengers,
acts as their main source of finances, and

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.580
as the supplier of all the stuff they tend
to break.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.680
He also has a knack for bringing in other
long-serving Avengers, like the arching Avenger

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.340
Hawkeye.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:56.340
Clint Barton first found his way into the
Marvel Universe in 1964's Tales of Suspense

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.160
#57.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.260
Enamored by the seductive Black Widow herself
a villain at the time Hawkeye fought Iron

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.460
Man to help her steal Stark's technology.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:11.599
A year later, in Avengers #16, Hawkeye became
a hero as part of the new roster of Avengers

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.720
along with Captain America and two other former
villains, Quicksilver and the Scarlet Witch.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.000
But just because Hawkeye was on the side of
the angels doesn't mean that he wouldn't fight

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.040
Iron Man again.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:28.560
Hawkeye joined the ranks of another super
team, the Defenders, right before 1973's Avengers/Defenders

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.340
War broke out.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.870
When the two teams squared off against each
other, it was Hawkeye and Iron Man who battled

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.520
in 1973's Defenders #9.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:37.920
"Just can't seem to miss."

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.600
"First time for everything"

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:42.740
"Made you look."

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.280
A true Hulkbuster

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:53.310
Tony Stark and Bruce Banner might be "science
bros" in the MCU, but the two have gone head

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.360
to head more times than most friends.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.660
Iron Man has even managed to get the upper
hand on a couple occasions.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:04.870
Iron Man's first and most memorable victory
over the Hulk occurred in 1980's Iron Man

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.800
#132.

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:12.100
In the issue, Iron Man put 100 percent of
his armor's energy into a single punch, and

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.860
with it he was able to K.O. the Green Goliath.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.060
Stark rendered the Hulk unconscious again
in 2009's Mighty Avengers #22 by blasting

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.260
the Hulk with an exploding rocket booster.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.480
Ironically, as successful as the Hulkbuster
suit was in Avengers: Age of Ultron, Iron

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.340
Man has never been able to defeat the Hulk
while wearing the Hulkbuster suit in the comics.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:39.180
Every Iron Man/Hulk fight involving the Hulkbuster
armor has ended in a cancelled fight, or with

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.960
the Hulk having busted the 'Buster.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:46.920
"I'm sorry."

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.100
The Thorbuster Armor

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:57.560
You hear a lot about Tony Stark's Hulkbuster
armor, but the Hulk isn't the only fellow

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.200
Avenger that Iron Man developed a specific
armor to counter.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:08.280
In Marvel's 2003 three-part mini-event Standoff,
Doctor Doom manipulated international events

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.360
to set Iron Man, Thor, and Captain America
against each other.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:17.260
Not knowing how else he could even stand a
chance, Stark created his Thorbuster suit.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.280
Powered by an Asgardian crystal that Thor
had previously given Stark as a gift, the

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:27.620
Thorbuster rig looked like a marriage between
Tony's classic red-and-gold suit and the Destroyer's

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.120
armor.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.000
But ultimately it wasn't enough.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:33.720
Thor destroyed the suit's reactor and Tony
ejected from the armor.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:38.580
The only thing that seems to get "busted"
when Tony pulls out a "blankbuster" suit in

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.920
the comics seems to be the suit itself.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.060
"Let's get you comfy.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:45.980
You happy now?"

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.200
Thanks for watching!

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.080
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

